# Copy to .env and adjust for your environment. Expo inlines any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the JS bundle at build time — never put
# secrets here (see MOBILE_INTEGRATION_AUDIT.md §38 / §11 / rules 6-7).
#
# Leave unset to fall back to src/config/env.ts's built-in dev/production
# resolution (see mobile/README.md for what that resolves to per platform).

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Google Sign-In (Android only for now). Set to the WEB OAuth client id
# (same value as the web app's NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID) — the native
# Credential Manager flow (react-native-nitro-google-signin, see
# GoogleSignInButton.tsx) returns an ID token audienced to this web client,
# which backend/services/google_auth.py already accepts.
# Also required in Google Cloud Console: an "Android" type OAuth client for
# package uz.gapirai.mobile with the signing key's SHA-1 (attestation only).
# Unset -> the Google button is hidden.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
